Both pass. Here's a summary of what changed:

**`index.html`**: moved `contacts-add-area` before `contacts-alpha`, so the "+ Add Contact" button renders above the A-Z index tabs.

**`src/ui/contacts.ts`**: updated the fallback DOM-creation order to match — alpha index is placed first, then the add-area is inserted before it.

**`src/styles/layout.css`** (header fix):
- Added `flex-wrap: wrap` to `header` so items can wrap at narrow widths.
- Made `h1` `flex: 1 1 auto` with `min-width: 0` and `text-overflow: ellipsis` so the title shrinks before it overflows.
- Made `#theme-toggle` `flex: 0 0 auto` so it never grows but wraps below the title if the row is too narrow.

**`src/styles/directory.css`** (directory row fix):
- Changed `.contact-row` to a 3-column grid (`minmax(0, 1fr) auto auto`) so the name column is bounded and can't push the phone off-screen.
- Added a `@media (max-width: 400px)` block that switches to 2-column, 2-row stacking: name/relation spans the full top row, phone and actions sit side-by-side on the row below.
- Removed `white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis` from `.contact-name` and replaced it with `overflow-wrap: break-word` so long names wrap rather than truncate or overflow.
- `.contact-phone` retains `white-space: nowrap` throughout, so numbers never break mid-digit.
